# Cross-Platform (Android / Desktop / iOS)

This game ships on **desktop, Android, and iOS**. Every feature, change, and helper must be **valid on all three** unless the user explicitly scopes work to one platform.

## Iron Law

Do not ship code that only works on a full JVM (desktop / Android). **iOS (RoboVM) is a first-class target.** Prefer the **intersection** of APIs that all three runtimes support.

RoboVM’s `robovm-rt` is roughly pre–Java 8 collections: desktop tests can be green while iOS dies with `NoSuchMethodError` / `NoClassDefFoundError`.

## RoboVM API policy (do not forget)

**Default: avoid unsupported APIs and rewrite to classic forms.** Do **not** grow a parallel JDK (`java.util.function` / `Optional` clones).

| Avoid on shared paths                   | Use instead                                                                     |
| --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `String.isBlank()`                      | `Strings.isBlank(s)` (multi-site helper)                                        |
| `String.join(...)`                      | `Strings.join(...)` when needed in several places; else a local `StringBuilder` |
| `java.util.Base64`                      | `Base64Codec` (same RFC 4648 strings — no DB/wire migration)                    |
| `java.util.function.*`                  | Local nested interface next to the owner, or existing `Callback`                |
| `java.util.Optional`                    | Nullable return / explicit empty collections                                    |
| `List.of` / `Map.of` / `Set.of`         | `Collections.emptyList()` / `emptyMap()` / `emptySet()`, or `new ArrayList<>()` |
| `list.sort(...)`                        | `Collections.sort(list, comparator)`                                            |
| `Comparator.comparing*`                 | Anonymous `Comparator` / `Integer.compare` / `Long.compare`                     |
| `Map.getOrDefault` / `Map.merge`        | `containsKey` / `get` + `put`                                                   |
| `Collection.removeIf`                   | Iterator remove loop                                                            |
| `java.nio.file` for game data           | `FileUtils` / `java.io` streams                                                 |
| Desktop-only env / cwd files at runtime | Build-time defaults + `FileUtils` Local                                         |

Shared helpers under `com.watabou.utils` only for **hot duplicates** (e.g. `Strings.isBlank`). One-off gaps: inline rewrite at the call site.

```java
// ❌ BAD — missing on RoboVM
if (body == null || body.isBlank()) { ... }
list.sort(Comparator.comparingInt(...));
return Optional.empty();
Function<String, String> env = System::getenv; // especially in <clinit>

// ✅ GOOD
if (Strings.isBlank(body)) { ... }
Collections.sort(list, new Comparator<JSONObject>() { ... });
return null; // or empty list
// local interface / Map test seam — not java.util.function
```

Guard: keep / extend `RoboVMUnsupportedApisTest` when adding new forbidden patterns.

## Default structure

- Put shared behavior in `core` (or `SPD-classes`) so all launchers get it.
- Do not assume a desktop JVM, mouse/keyboard-only input, large screen, or process cwd.
- Prefer portable APIs (`FileUtils`, libGDX, `Game.platform`, `Strings`, `Callback`, existing UI).

## Before finishing any feature or change

Ask: “Does this still work on Android, desktop, and iOS — including the APIs used?”

- [ ] Logic lives in `core` / `SPD-classes` (or each launcher is updated intentionally)
- [ ] No JDK APIs RoboVM lacks (table above); no new `java.util.function` / `Optional` in production
- [ ] No desktop-only assumptions (cwd files, `System.exit` paths, mouse-only UX, unbounded RAM)
- [ ] Touch + keyboard/mouse still usable where UI changed
- [ ] Portrait and landscape considered if layout/UI changed
- [ ] Network / threading / lifecycle safe on mobile (pause, background, slow I/O)
- [ ] Persistence uses `FileUtils` Local — not raw `java.io.File` relative paths

## File persistence

Launchers set `FileUtils.setDefaultFileProperties(Files.FileType.Local, "")`. Game data must use that sandbox on every platform.

```java
// ❌ BAD — process cwd; breaks on Android/iOS
new FileOutputStream("echoes-solo/depth-5.dat");

// ✅ GOOD
FileUtils.bundleToFile("echoes-solo/depth-5.dat", bundle);
```

## Exceptions

- Launcher modules (`android/`, `ios/`, `desktop/`) may use native APIs.
- Platform-specific work only when the user asks for it; note which platforms are out of scope.
